From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Radio Sound <opensource@radiosound.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 04:35:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] caremu: use VirtIO-compatible input parameters

Copyright 2026 Radio Sound, Inc.
Licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

The Android 16 car emulator audio HAL opens its capture stream with
PCM_MONOTONIC and an INT_MAX stop threshold. The VirtIO sound device exposed by
the Android Emulator rejects those input parameters, so the input worker exits
and every AudioRecord read is zero-filled. tinycap can capture from the same
device with the default stop threshold and without the monotonic flag.

This is an emulator-only compatibility patch. Raspberry Pi products do not
inherit the caremu HAL or this source path.
---
 device/generic/car/emulator/audio/driver/audio_hw.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/device/generic/car/emulator/audio/driver/audio_hw.c b/device/generic/car/emulator/audio/driver/audio_hw.c
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/device/generic/car/emulator/audio/driver/audio_hw.c
+++ b/device/generic/car/emulator/audio/driver/audio_hw.c
@@ -237,4 +237,4 @@ static struct pcm_config pcm_config_in = {
     .format = PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE,
     .start_threshold = 0,
-    .stop_threshold = INT_MAX,
+    .stop_threshold = 0,
 };
@@ -986,7 +986,7 @@ static void *in_read_worker(void *args) {
         }
         if (!pcm) {
             pcm = pcm_open(PCM_CARD, PCM_DEVICE,
-                    PCM_IN | PCM_MONOTONIC, &in->pcm_config);
+                    PCM_IN, &in->pcm_config);
             if (!pcm_is_ready(pcm)) {
                 ALOGE("pcm_open(in) failed: %s: channels %d format %d rate %d",
                         pcm_get_error(pcm),
--
